==============================================================================
FEATURES				*competitest-features*

- Multi-language support: Works with C, C++, Rust, Java, Python (configurable)
- Flexible workflow: No strict naming rules. Optional folder structures
- Configurable: Global and per-folder settings (|competitest-local-config|)
- Testcase storage: Single file or multiple text files
- Testcase management: Add/edit/delete testcases easily
- Interactive testing: Run all tests with visual results
- Platform integration: Download from competitive programming sites
- Templates: For problems and contests
- Output diff: Compare actual vs expected output
- Statusline and winbar integration
- Customizable highlight groups

==============================================================================
USAGE					*competitest-usage*

To load this plugin with default configuration, call `setup()`: >lua
	require('competitest').setup()
<
To customize settings: >lua
	require('competitest').setup {
		-- put here configuration
	}
<
USAGE NOTES				*competitest-usage-notes*

- Programs must read from stdin and write to stdout
- Testcases require input; expected output is optional
- Testcases can be stored as multiple files or a single msgpack file
  via `testcases_use_single_file` (default: false). With
  `testcases_auto_detect_storage`, the format is auto-detected

STORING TESTCASES			*competitest-storing-testcases*

Default naming (source: task-A.cpp): >
    task-A0.in    [Input]
    task-A0.ans   [Expected output]
<
Customize via: >
    testcases_input_file_format
    testcases_output_file_format
<
Set `testcases_use_single_file` to true to store all testcases in one file
(default: `task-A.testcases`). Customizable via `testcases_single_file_format`
and `testcases_directory`.

COMMANDS				*competitest-commands*

Execute with source buffer focused:

Command                          Action ~
:CompetiTest add_testcase        Add new testcase
:CompetiTest edit_testcase [x]   Edit testcase (optional number)
:CompetiTest delete_testcase [x] Remove testcase (optional number)
:CompetiTest convert             Convert testcase to single or multiple files
:CompetiTest run                 Run all testcases (compile and execute)
:CompetiTest run_no_compile      Run without compiling
:CompetiTest show_ui             Show UI without re-running

TESTCASE EDITOR CONTROLS		*competitest-editor-controls*

Key Binding            Action ~
<C-h>, <C-l>, <C-i>    Switch between input/output windows
<C-s>                  Save and close
:wq                    Save and close

TESTCASE RUNNER CONTROLS		*competitest-runner-controls*

Key    Action ~
R      Re-run current testcase
<C-r>  Re-run all testcases
K      Kill current testcase process
<C-k>  Kill all processes
i/I    View input (current/all)
a/A    View expected output (current/all)
o/O    View stdout (current/all)
e/E    View stderr (current/all)
d/D    Toggle diff view (current/all)
q/Q    Close UI

==============================================================================
RECEIVING TESTCASES			*competitest-receiving*

REQUIREMENT: competitive-companion browser extension
    https://github.com/jmerle/competitive-companion

Command                            Action ~
:CompetiTest receive testcases     Receive single testcase set
:CompetiTest receive problem       Receive problem (creates source file)
:CompetiTest receive contest       Receive entire contest
:CompetiTest receive persistently  Receive testcases, problems and contests persistently
:CompetiTest receive status        Show reception status
:CompetiTest receive stop          Stop receiving

After running this command, click green "+" in browser extension.

CUSTOM FOLDER STRUCTURE			*competitest-custom-folder*

Example configurations: >vim9
    received_problems_path = "$(HOME)/CP/$(JUDGE)/$(CONTEST)/$(PROBLEM).$(FEXT)"
    received_contests_directory = "$(HOME)/CP/$(JUDGE)/$(CONTEST)"
    received_contests_problems_path = "$(PROBLEM)/main.$(FEXT)"
<

TEMPLATES				*competitest-templates*

Enable with `template_file` option. C++ example: >cpp
    // Problem: $(PROBLEM)
    // Contest: $(CONTEST)
    // Judge: $(JUDGE)
    // URL: $(URL)
    // Memory: $(MEMLIM)
    // Time: $(TIMELIM)
    // Start: $(DATE)

    #include <iostream>
    using namespace std;
    int main() {
        cout << "Template for $(PROBLEM)" << endl;
        return 0;
    }
<

==============================================================================
CONFIGURATION				*competitest-configuration*

LOCAL CONFIGURATION			*competitest-local-config*

This name can be changed configuring the option `local_config_file_name`.

Create `.competitest.lua` in project folder: >lua
	return {
		multiple_testing = 3,
		maximum_time = 2500,
		testcases_input_file_format = "in_$(TCNUM).txt",
		testcases_output_file_format = "ans_$(TCNUM).txt",
		testcases_single_file_format = "$(FNOEXT).tc",
	}
<

MODIFIERS				*competitest-modifiers*

FILE FORMAT MODIFIERS ~
$(HOME)       User home directory
$(FNAME)      Full filename
$(FNOEXT)     Filename without extension
$(FEXT)       File extension
$(FABSPATH)   Absolute file path
$(ABSDIR)     Absolute directory path
$(TCNUM)      Testcase number

RECEIVE MODIFIERS ~
$(CWD)        Current directory
$(PROBLEM)    Problem name
$(JUDGE)      Platform name (Codeforces, etc.)
$(CONTEST)    Contest name
$(URL)        Problem URL
$(MEMLIM)     Memory limit
$(TIMELIM)    Time limit
$(DATE)       Current date/time

==============================================================================
DEFAULT CONFIGURATION			*competitest-default-config*

Full configuration: >lua
	require('competitest').setup {
		local_config_file_name = ".competitest.lua",

		floating_border = "rounded",
		floating_border_highlight = "FloatBorder",
		picker_ui = {
			width = 0.2,
			height = 0.3,
			mappings = {
				focus_next = { "j", "<down>", "<Tab>" },
				focus_prev = { "k", "<up>", "<S-Tab>" },
				close = { "<esc>", "<C-c>", "q", "Q" },
				submit = "<cr>",
			},
		},
		editor_ui = {
			popup_width = 0.4,
			popup_height = 0.6,
			show_nu = true,
			show_rnu = false,
			normal_mode_mappings = {
				switch_window = { "<C-h>", "<C-l>", "<C-i>" },
				save_and_close = "<C-s>",
				cancel = { "q", "Q" },
			},
			insert_mode_mappings = {
				switch_window = { "<C-h>", "<C-l>", "<C-i>" },
				save_and_close = "<C-s>",
				cancel = "<C-q>",
			},
		},
		runner_ui = {
			interface = "popup",
			selector_show_nu = false,
			selector_show_rnu = false,
			show_nu = true,
			show_rnu = false,
			mappings = {
				run_again = "R",
				run_all_again = "<C-r>",
				kill = "K",
				kill_all = "<C-k>",
				view_input = { "i", "I" },
				view_output = { "a", "A" },
				view_stdout = { "o", "O" },
				view_stderr = { "e", "E" },
				toggle_diff = { "d", "D" },
				close = { "q", "Q" },
			},
			viewer = {
				width = 0.5,
				height = 0.5,
				show_nu = true,
				show_rnu = false,
				open_when_compilation_fails = true,
			},
		},
		popup_ui = {
			total_width = 0.8,
			total_height = 0.8,
			layout = {
				{ 4, "tc" },
				{ 5, { { 1, "so" }, { 1, "si" } } },
				{ 5, { { 1, "eo" }, { 1, "se" } } },
			},
		},
		split_ui = {
			position = "right",
			relative_to_editor = true,
			total_width = 0.3,
			vertical_layout = {
				{ 1, "tc" },
				{ 1, { { 1, "so" }, { 1, "eo" } } },
				{ 1, { { 1, "si" }, { 1, "se" } } },
			},
			total_height = 0.4,
			horizontal_layout = {
				{ 2, "tc" },
				{ 3, { { 1, "so" }, { 1, "si" } } },
				{ 3, { { 1, "eo" }, { 1, "se" } } },
			},
		},

		save_current_file = true,
		save_all_files = false,
		compile_directory = ".",
		compile_command = {
			c = { exec = "gcc", args = { "-Wall", "$(FNAME)", "-o", "$(FNOEXT)" } },
			cpp = { exec = "g++", args = { "-Wall", "$(FNAME)", "-o", "$(FNOEXT)" } },
			rust = { exec = "rustc", args = { "$(FNAME)" } },
			java = { exec = "javac", args = { "$(FNAME)" } },
		},
		running_directory = ".",
		run_command = {
			c = { exec = "./$(FNOEXT)" },
			cpp = { exec = "./$(FNOEXT)" },
			rust = { exec = "./$(FNOEXT)" },
			python = { exec = "python", args = { "$(FNAME)" } },
			java = { exec = "java", args = { "$(FNOEXT)" } },
		},
		multiple_testing = -1,
		maximum_time = 5000,
		output_compare_method = "squish",
		view_output_diff = false,

		testcases_directory = ".",
		testcases_use_single_file = false,
		testcases_auto_detect_storage = true,
		testcases_single_file_format = "$(FNOEXT).testcases",
		testcases_input_file_format = "$(FNOEXT)_input$(TCNUM).txt",
		testcases_output_file_format = "$(FNOEXT)_output$(TCNUM).txt",

		companion_port = 27121,
		receive_print_message = true,
		start_receiving_persistently_on_setup = false,
		template_file = false,
		evaluate_template_modifiers = false,
		date_format = "%c",
		received_files_extension = "cpp",
		received_problems_path = "$(CWD)/$(PROBLEM).$(FEXT)",
		received_problems_prompt_path = true,
		received_contests_directory = "$(CWD)",
		received_contests_problems_path = "$(PROBLEM).$(FEXT)",
		received_contests_prompt_directory = true,
		received_contests_prompt_extension = true,
		open_received_problems = true,
		open_received_contests = true,
		replace_received_testcases = false,
	}
<
==============================================================================
CONFIGURATION EXPLANATION		*competitest-config-explanation*

local_config_file_name			*competitest-config-local_config_file_name*
  Type: string
  Default: ".competitest.lua"
  Per-folder configuration filename. See |competitest-local-config|


floating_border			*competitest-config-floating_border*
  Type: string
  Default: "rounded"
  Border style for floating windows.
  See: https://github.com/MunifTanjim/nui.nvim/tree/main/lua/nui/popup#borderstyle


floating_border_highlight	*competitest-config-floating_border_highlight*
  Type: string
  Highlight group used for popup borders


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PICKER UI					*competitest-config-picker_ui*

picker_ui				*competitest-config-picker_ui*
  Type: dictionary
  Testcase picker UI settings

picker_ui.width			*competitest-config-picker_ui-width*
  Type: number
  Width ratio (0–1) relative to Neovim window

picker_ui.height			*competitest-config-picker_ui-height*
  Type: number
  Height ratio (0–1) relative to Neovim window

picker_ui.mappings		*competitest-config-picker_ui-mappings*
  Type: dictionary
  Key mappings for interacting with picker UI


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
EDITOR UI					*competitest-config-editor_ui*

editor_ui				*competitest-config-editor_ui*
  Type: dictionary
  Testcase editor UI settings

editor_ui.popup_width		*competitest-config-editor_ui-popup_width*
  Type: number
  Width ratio (0–1) of popup editor

editor_ui.popup_height		*competitest-config-editor_ui-popup_height*
  Type: number
  Height ratio (0–1) of popup editor

editor_ui.show_nu			*competitest-config-editor_ui-show_nu*
  Type: boolean
  Show line numbers

editor_ui.show_rnu		*competitest-config-editor_ui-show_rnu*
  Type: boolean
  Show relative line numbers

editor_ui.switch_window		*competitest-config-editor_ui-switch_window*
  Type: mapping
  Switch between input/output windows

editor_ui.save_and_close		*competitest-config-editor_ui-save_and_close*
  Type: mapping
  Save testcase and close editor

editor_ui.cancel			*competitest-config-editor_ui-cancel*
  Type: mapping
  Close editor without saving


------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNNER UI					*competitest-config-runner_ui*

runner_ui				*competitest-config-runner_ui*
  Type: dictionary
  Testcase runner UI settings

runner_ui.interface		*competitest-config-runner_ui-interface*
  Type: string
  Default: "popup"
  Interface type: "popup" or "split"

runner_ui.selector_show_nu	*competitest-config-runner_ui-selector_show_nu*
  Type: boolean
  Show line numbers in selector

runner_ui.selector_show_rnu	*competitest-config-runner_ui-selector_show_rnu*
  Type: boolean
  Show relative line numbers in selector

runner_ui.show_nu		*competitest-config-runner_ui-show_nu*
  Type: boolean
  Show line numbers in detail windows

runner_ui.show_rnu		*competitest-config-runner_ui-show_rnu*
  Type: boolean
  Show relative line numbers in detail windows

runner_ui.mappings		*competitest-config-runner_ui-mappings*
  Type: dictionary
  Key mappings in runner UI:
      run_again:      Re-run current testcase
      run_all_again:  Re-run all testcases
      kill:           Kill current process
      kill_all:       Kill all processes
      view_input:     View input
      view_output:    View expected output
      view_stdout:    View stdout
      view_stderr:    View stderr
      toggle_diff:    Toggle diff view
      close:          Close UI

runner_ui.viewer			*competitest-config-runner_ui-viewer*
  Type: dictionary
  Viewer window settings

runner_ui.viewer.width		*competitest-config-runner_ui-viewer-width*
  Type: number
  Width ratio (0–1)

runner_ui.viewer.height		*competitest-config-runner_ui-viewer-height*
  Type: number
  Height ratio (0–1)

runner_ui.viewer.show_nu		*competitest-config-runner_ui-viewer-show_nu*
  Type: boolean
  Show line numbers in viewer

runner_ui.viewer.show_rnu	*competitest-config-runner_ui-viewer-show_rnu*
  Type: boolean
  Show relative line numbers in viewer

runner_ui.viewer.open_when_compilation_fails
			*competitest-config-runner_ui-viewer-open_when_compilation_fails*
  Type: boolean
  Open viewer when compilation fails


